{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1430170-hakaken","id":1430170,"title":"Hakaken","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-12-27T19:32:11-08:00","id":1430170,"title":"Hakaken","content":"Was Hakaken ever developed elsewhere besides the totem description for the Black Spiral Dancers? That brief description has a lot of intriguing information. Below is from the second edition Book of the Wyrm - it has some details left out in other sources.<br /> <br /> We're told that he was a great Shadow Lord Ahroun who lead his tribe to victory against the Wyrm for over forty years. But in his hubris he danced the Labyrinth to show he could overcome it, became corrupt, and became an Incarna (!) when he finally advanced to its center. We're also interestingly told that some cults of Shadow Lords secretely worship him.<br /> <br /> Do we know anything about him prior to this fall? It seems Hakaken must have lived after the fall of the White Howlers. I also don't think he's mentioned in any of the Dark Ages materials, so he might have lived in the past 750 years.<br /> <br /> That he became an Incarna is interesting enough, but more surprising that he was a Shadow Lord. I would have naturally assumed any such Garou totem would have been one of the original White Howlers, but that isn't so. That may explain why some Shadow Lords worship him in secret. I would have thought that would have been interesting to develop in one of the tribebooks, but I don't remember him ever being mentioned. I think BotW2e came out after the original tribebook, and in Revised such evil camps were being purged. But I think it would be an interesting faction to depict - they have to be getting something from Hakaken to risk it. Is this ever mentioned elsewhere?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-09T00:21:14-08:00","id":1431539,"title":"","content":"I am taking that zero replies means nothing more is stated in any of the books. Which leaves any development to us. So let's do so. If this interests you, please post your comments and ideas!<br /> <br /> I think Shadow Lords who worship Hakaken are in two main categories. The first are those Shadow Lords close to falling to the Wyrm, or actually doing so. They're in the process of rejecting Gaia and Grandfather Thunder and putting their bets elsewhere. The second are Shadow Lords in the Bringers of Light camp. These Shadow Lords believe they can seek out the temptation of the Wyrm and defeat it, and thereby strengthen their soul. These could worship Hakaken, maybe even have him as a pack totem, yet stay &quot;true&quot; to Gaia. I doubt it, but that would be their justification.<br /> <br /> Hakaken is a powerful pack totem. His children get two Gifts and an extra die for Intimidation rolls. And it is said they believe he has &quot;further powers to bestow.&quot; Plus that a (ex-) tribemate has become an Incarna is probably a powerful incentive/inspiration.<br /> <br /> That's reason for some packs to think by being Hakaken's children they can help the tribe assume control of the Garou Nation (at least in second edition before Revised eliminated all these interesting things).<br /> <br /> Of course, one issue that needs addressing is if you're a Shadow Lord that is &quot;loyal&quot; to the tribe, but have Hakaken as a totem, how exactly do you hide this from your tribemates and the rest of the Garou? One's pack totem doesn't necessarily need to be nearby in the Penumbra. So maybe the totem not being around isn't a big deal. Or maybe the pack totem has means/powers to hide its true appearance or Wyrm taint so other Garou aren't suspicious. Enough Totem points can justify a lot of things. And unusual totems aren't necessarily suspicious given all the totems mentioned in tribebooks and the Rage books. Still, I think these Shadow Lords need to describe/lie their totems as something else when speaking to other Garou. I wonder what would be good cover stories, as they shouldn't be spirits of Grandfather Thunder's brood or common spirits that could tell other Garou, &quot;You know, I don't know any spirits of that type that know ANYTHING about that pack despite being broodmates.&quot; Or maybe the spirit is able to disguise itself enough that it can fool other spirits as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-09T01:03:48-08:00","id":1431541,"title":"","content":"That\u2019s interesting. I\u2019ve only read the Revised Shadow Lord tribebook (and I don\u2019t remember seeing Hakaken in the W20 Book of the Wyrm), but I really Like this. Would the followers of Hakaken have been purged after Yuri Konietzko took control of the Shadow Lords during the Revised era? Or maybe just driven underground (literally)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-09T11:16:34-08:00","id":1431592,"title":"","content":"I think they would have always been underground (not literally) so Yuri would have had to somehow find them first. But he could certainly make it a priority to uncover and suppress the secret cults of Hakaken.<br /> <br /> So it again goes to the question if there are packs of Hakaken, how are they able to disguise themselves? Is this something that would be hard or easy to do? I haven't thought my way through this sufficiently to answer yet.<br /> <br /> There's also the idea that Shadow Lords could worship Hakaken, but it might not be as a pack totem, but through other means (though I am not sure what that might mean in Werewolf terms - do they summon spirits and donate Gnosis? Just do things like set up hidden shrines? Simply ask for his aid in their hearts and minds?)<br /> <br /> Since the cult does not seem to have been described, we have a lot of leeway. I think for the cult to exist in the first place, it has to be hard to detect them.<br /> <br /> I also think it's important to know how Hakaken is spoken of inside the tribe normally. He was after all one of the greatest Shadow Lord ahrouns before his fall, and there are probably lots of stories that he is involved in. There's a good chance he was of Legendary rank. So it's probably impossible to simply not talk about him. It'd be like talking about the Battle of Saratoga without mentioning Benedict Arnold. Even if they don't use his name and use some kind of euphemism (like how &quot;He Who Is Not To Be Named&quot; is used as substitute for Voldemort in the Harry Potter world), it just makes it even more obvious who he is and the power of his name. If you don't talk about all of these events that this great hero of the Shadow Lords did, you must end up avoiding an entire time period of the tribe. And that might do things like create even more curiosity about it, or anger Ancestor spirits who were witnesses or participants of events, or other spirits. So I think the Shadow Lords must still talk about him, but use other rhetorical tricks to undermine his character in order to not make him be attractive to impressionable Shadow Lords. Of course, that must not entirely succeed since he has secret cults.<br /> <br /> There's also the possibility that before Hakaken fell, he had already left behind a significant family of Garou and kinfolk. And therefore a not insignificant number of Shadow Lords today can point to him being their ancestor. Maybe his descendants are too numerous and too politically powerful to suppress. But some of them might be more susceptible to wanting to honor their ancestor who is now an Incarna than others, and this is one reason why these secret cults persist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-05T20:13:23-08:00","id":1438228,"title":"","content":"It isn't that hard to undermine his character. He became a Black Spiral Dancer!<br /> <br /> But yeah, just because the tribes* tried to kill off their fallen and nearly-fallen members, doesn't mean they fully succeeded.<br /> <br /> *Other than the effing Red Talons, who protect them instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-05T21:05:37-08:00","id":1438243,"title":"","content":"Of course, but if all you say is &quot;He became a Black Spiral Dancer&quot;, it might backfire on you. If stories about Hakaken are about how much he kicks ass, but then he became a BSD; it might cause an inappropriate lesson that &quot;hey, maybe becoming a BSD isn't too bad since kickass Hakaken became one!&quot; So you have to emphasize undesirable traits even in the stories when he was still a great Garou hero so people don't try to emulate him.<br /> <br /> A big question is what are the nature of the Shadow Lord cults that worship Hakaken. Are they all Garou who either don't mind serving the Wyrm in actuality or potentially? Or are they deluded into thinking they can still serve Gaia while worshiping Hakaken? Maybe both? Is there an Ancesor component to this? There is potentially a lot to explore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-07T10:54:14-08:00","id":1438476,"title":"","content":"Hakaken is a figure of pride so great it led to his damnation. In his overwhelming arrogance, he thought he could outwit a member of the Triat and gain awesone power.<br /> <br /> Well, he was right about the awesome power, but <i>very</i> wrong about outwitting the Wyrm. To gain his Incarna status, Hakaken had to betray virtually everything he once cherished to gain godhood.<br /> <br /> He's a cautionary tale. <i>Not</i> a success story. Power for its own sake leads to ruination,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-07T12:29:19-08:00","id":1438489,"title":"","content":"Since we don't know any details of Hakaken's story, what you said could be true. But it might also be very different. The Garou would say Hakaken was ruined and not a success story because by their definition, falling to the Wyrm means failure. But the actual story might not actually lead to that interpretation. People say treason never prospers. But that is just an aphorism. As John Harrington says, &quot;Treason doth never prosper: what 's the reason? Why, if it prosper, none dare call it treason.&quot;<br /> <br /> Let's look at the story of Darth Vader as an example. As a result of his turning to the Dark Side, the woman he loved died, he was horrifically burned, spent the rest of his life crippled in an iron lung, had his most cherished beliefs (in the Force) ridiculed by everyone around him, and became an errand boy for the Emperor. Vader clearly lost a lot in his decision to betray he Jedi. That is a cautionary tale.<br /> <br /> But let's look at another famous cinematic traitor, Jake Sully from Avatar. He gets the girl, becomes leader of a new people, and enjoys all the benefits thereby. And of course the audience is encouraged to view his betrayal as all good. Likewise, in history we can find all sorts of people who benefitted from their treason. The societies they betrayed still have good reason to disparage them, but it would be wrong to say that their treason lead to their ruination.<br /> <br /> So what is the case with Hakaken? We don't know. We're not given enough details. We only know he became an Incarna. We don't know if the price involved the destruction of the things he care most about like a Darklord in Ravenloft being simultaneously cursed and blessed by the Dark Powers. That's a possibility, and an ST could develop Hakaken's story that way. That would be cool. People like villains like that - Strahd von Zarovich, Lord Soth in Dragonlance, Darth Vader. They are interesting and compelling because they are tragic, but powerful and evil.<br /> <br /> But it's not the only model, and it is possible Hakaken's story is very different. It's not even necessarily true that Hakaken lost who he was by Dancing the Spiral and turned into something he hated. One possible interpretation is that Hakaken knew exactly what was he was doing, accepted the price, and succeeded. That would make him a colossal jerk who always put himself ahead of Gaia, but that's not uncommon. He'd be more like General Zod from Superman II. &quot;Kneel before Hakaken sons of Gaia!&quot; This would <i>also</i> make him a very interesting villain, and we could see why other Shadow Lords would want to emulate him. (Perhaps they even tell themselves that Hakaken intends to do a face turn in the Apocalypse and rejoin Gaia. People are all sorts of stupid or tell themselves lies so they can justify being self-serving.)<br /> <br /> Either could work, but they'd lead to very different cults. Or we might say that the first story is true and Garou are right, but that Hakaken's cultists believe the second story is true; or vice versa. Or there might be an entirely different story and angle to the cults.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-20T12:45:26-07:00","id":1551161,"title":"","content":"I'm resurrecting another old thread of mine. I'm still intrigued by the idea that there are certain &quot;cults&quot; of Hakaken within the Shadow Lords hoping to receive further gifts. It's something I've wanted to incorporate into my chronicles and trying to figure out the best way to do it.<br /> <br /> I think there are several &quot;obvious&quot; ways to proceed.<br /> <br /> First, Hakaken likely has many descendants among the Shadow Lords. He was a great tribal leader for forty years. He probably sired a lot of children. Hakaken would be a possible Ancestor spirit for some of them. Depending on the player and ST, maybe that only happens as a result of a botch on their Ancestors roll, or because of a Flaw like Insane Ancestor, Cursed, or Taint of Corruption. Or even perhaps as the Merit Ancestor Ally! That could be a very interesting relationship for the character to play out. In fact, if I ever create another PC maybe I'll try to convince the ST to allow this (I imagine some won't). This is perhaps the least likely to be punished even if discovered because it's not exactly something the character can choose. It just happens to her.<br /> <br /> Second, I recently learned that Hakaken was once a member of the Masks camp (this is mentioned in the original Werewolf Players Guide). The Masks is a camp all about using fear as a weapon. I imagine this camp came about because the dark skies of Thunder can hide people, and the unknown tends to generate fear. Plus there is a strong association between Shadow Lords and fear spirits in general. Hakaken, &quot;the Master of Fear&quot;, likely learned his trained in the Masks, and he probably was a big mentor to other Shadow Lords in it. He was probably a respected elder and mentor in the camp. Even after his fall, he might still be a respected (though no longer admired) figure. I could see some members choosing to continue their studies under Hakaken although obviously in secret. It's a dangerous pursuit, but the Shadow Lords have done far worse.<br /> <br /> Third, the Bringers of Light camp is about developing &quot;inner strength&quot; by testing themselves against the taint around them. They cooperate with vampires, have prolonged stays in BSD Hives, and undertake long journeys in Wyrm corrupted umbral realms. I could see packs within this group even having Hakaken as a pack totem. What better way to test yourself? (maybe not, but it's what the camp is about)<br /> <br /> Fourth, if there are Shadow Lords who devoted themselves to redeeming Bat, certainly there is precedence for Shadow Lords who associate with Hakaken because they want to redeem him. How can you blame them anymore than you would blame the pack(s) who tried to redeem Bat? Just because they haven't succeeded yet doesn't mean they won't... at some point in time.<br /> <br /> Now for this to work, I imagine Hakaken must not be a moustache twirling villain when he appears. Yes, he'll be spooky, probably terrifying to approach, but he won't be cartoonish in his allegiance to the Wyrm. He'll likely present himself as a much more neutral figure focused on the arts of fear who is always open to those who are worthy to learn his secrets about fear. Someone still sympathetic to his old ties as a mortal to his tribe (descendants and camp mates).<br /> <br /> Obviously the tribe as a whole will not advertise the fact that there are secret cults of Hakaken inside the tribe. That is just bad PR. And among the Shadow Lords, you will have all sorts of opinions. Many will be outraged at any such cults because it smacks of treason. However, I do think - given what we know about the tribe - there is more than enough tribal tradition that some can justify their activities with the Incarna. It'll be hard to go after them without a lot of collateral damage in the tribe of all the other shady stuff they do. As such, I think this could very well be a &quot;don't ask, don't tell&quot; situation throughout the tribe with activities handled on a case by case basis. Like with many World of Darkness examples, &quot;don't get caught&quot; is the primary rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-20T13:43:18-07:00","id":1551162,"title":"","content":"Even if Hakaken personally had a lot of kids, Shadow Lords are doubly afflicted with some less than encouraging turnover rates on account of 1) being Garou and 2) being in an environment with even more pronounced jockeying for power and influence (i.e. being Shadow Lords). So it's really anyone's guess if he's an ancestor, and he's probably not accessible via Ancestors due to being completely and utterly changed into an Incarna... though there might still be a fragment left, and it might even be the hook they need like how they won over a bit of Bat. If he's still accessible and liable to corrupt descendants, that's another strike on having living descendants, as they'd either end up crashing out from Wyrm influence, being accused of it on account of their lineage and set up for lethal failure (even regular failure for Shadow Lords is probably enough to ensure that they don't get any among Kinfolk and their lineage is likely severed), or have no kids at all because of self-loathing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-21T01:36:37-07:00","id":1551180,"title":"","content":"To be fair Hakaken wouldn't be that strange to be followed<br /> I mean Grandfather Thudner himself hands out gifts to mask your Taint... (also if you are in to crossovers, he took the Danislav ravenant family under his dark wings and his servants teach gifts to them up to level 3!)<br /> Typhon is a destructive quasy-dark totem of War, &quot;a rampaging dragon spirit&quot;<br /> The Hakken's not that nice optional totem, Susanowo<i>, </i>the Lord of Rain and Storms (not the same as Grandfather, they call him Naru-kami) is speculated to be tainted<br /> Even the original Shadow Lord Totem - before they quietly shifted to Grandfather - , Raven (or Crow, I always mix them up...) wasn't that &quot;nice and pure&quot; (I can't really remember but I think he even passed over the whole tribe to his Boss, Grandpa' as part of a plan) - carion bird, eater of dead, shadowy and sneaky, borderline tainted himself<br /> Hakaken is not even in the worst three if you think about it<br /> Redeeming him is a totally valid agenda like following him (not publically) and he probably a valid Ancestor spirit too - I would certainly allow him<br /> Actually I would treat him a Great Uktena, Black Pegasus or a bloody cannibal spirit of the winter Wendigo (so long og Sasquatch totem, we hardly knew you) level of of shady, dark Totem<br /> But since Shadow Lords are regularly deal wih the Spirits of Fear and Spirits of Darkness I doubt enyone even would notice who is that pack's patron","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 05-21-2025, 04:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-21T10:11:26-07:00","id":1551196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1430170-hakaken?p=1551180#post1551180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair Hakaken wouldn't be that strange to be followed<br /> I mean Grandfather Thudner himself hands out gifts to mask your Taint... (also if you are in to crossovers, he took the Danislav ravenant family under his dark wings and his servants teach gifts to them up to level 3!)<br /> Typhon is a destructive quasy-dark totem of War, &quot;a rampaging dragon spirit&quot;<br /> The Hakken's not that nice optional totem, Susanowo<i>, </i>the Lord of Rain and Storms (not the same as Grandfather, they call him Naru-kami) is speculated to be tainted<br /> Even the original Shadow Lord Totem - before they quietly shifted to Grandfather - , Raven (or Crow, I always mix them up...) wasn't that &quot;nice and pure&quot; (I can't really remember but I think he even passed over the whole tribe to his Boss, Grandpa' as part of a plan) - carion bird, eater of dead, shadowy and sneaky, borderline tainted himself<br /> Hakaken is not even in the worst three if you think about it<br /> Redeeming him is a totally valid agenda like following him (not publically) and he probably a valid Ancestor spirit too - I would certainly allow him<br /> Actually I would treat him a Great Uktena, Black Pegasus or a bloody cannibal spirit of the winter Wendigo (so long og Sasquatch totem, we hardly knew you) level of of shady, dark Totem<br /> But since Shadow Lords are regularly deal wih the Spirits of Fear and Spirits of Darkness I doubt enyone even would notice who is that pack's patron</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a lot like W5's treatment of Fly, which has reminders of why gnolls exist as they do in D&amp;D - creator doesn't like them and thinks they're the ick, presents them as being clearly evil or otherwise up to no good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-21T12:45:16-07:00","id":1551199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1430170-hakaken?p=1551180#post1551180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean Grandfather Thudner himself hands out gifts to mask your Taint...</div> </div> </div> </div>What Gift is that and what sourcebook? I would guess it's a camp Gift of the Bringers of Light.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1430170-hakaken?p=1551180#post1551180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Typhon is a destructive quasy-dark totem of War, &quot;a rampaging dragon spirit&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Typhon is a bit strange. That spirit was going to betray Grandfather Thunder and defect to the Wyrm in Rage Across Russia, and was a plot point in that sourcebook. When the spirit reappeared in the Revised tribebook, the totem description was completely changed and no mention of its loyalty made. I think that was part of a deliberate policy in Revised to eliminate any &quot;internal enemies&quot; among the Garou. So this traitorous spirit was completely retconned.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1430170-hakaken?p=1551180#post1551180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually I would treat him a Great Uktena, Black Pegasus or a bloody cannibal spirit of the winter Wendigo (so long og Sasquatch totem, we hardly knew you) level of of shady, dark Totem<br /> But since Shadow Lords are regularly deal wih the Spirits of Fear and Spirits of Darkness I doubt enyone even would notice who is that pack's patron</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that he willingly serves the Wyrm unlike the other spirits.<br /> <br /> Grandfather Thunder is a bit of a tyrant among the spirits, and he represents a lot of the darker aspects of nature. So he and his spirit brood allow a lot of things the other tribes don't. However, he's always been loyal to Gaia. Hakaken crosses the line in that respect. He's not part of Thunder's brood.<br /> <br /> However, I do think one reason such Hakaken cults exist among the Shadow Lords is that various Lords can argue it's OK because we already do &quot;X&quot;, and we all know that's fine so how is this different? I'm not <i>really</i> serving the Wyrm. I'm just using Hakaken to get some good spirit lore about fear so I can use it against other Wyrm minions. I know what I'm doing so don't worry about it.<br /> <br /> Of course, some Shadow Lords may be outright traitorous and intend to defect, but there is always a certain number of Garou from all tribes who do that. While an option, it is probably the least interesting thing for an ST to do with Hakaken cults.<br /> <br /> I don't think the tribe is riddled with Hakaken cults. Most tribe members probably won't have anything to do with him. However, besides the small number of cultists, there probably are a greater number of Lords who wouldn't snitch or investigate if they heard about it. They may think some dabbling is fine if it makes sense, and if certain lines aren't crossed. Having this as a mystery among the local Shadow Lords in the occasional chronicle isn't a bad idea. Just don't go overboard and have it in all chronicles, or place Hakaken cultists where they wouldn't make much sense.<br /> <br /> After a few online games, and running a tabletop chronicle of my own, I decided it was very hard for Philodox to earn Honor relative to Garou earning Glory and Wisdom. As a normal part of the game, there just seems to be many more opportunities to earn Glory and Wisdom than there are to earn Honor. As a result, I decided there needed to a be a certain level of scandalous or even criminal behavior among Garou so that Philodox (in particular, the other auspices usually can scrape up enough Honor that they need - at least until Elder rank) can pick up the Honor that they need. They need behavior they can expose and correct. They need disputes they can mediate. They need to speak truth to power even if it disrupts the sept or tribe to hear it.<br /> <br /> The game needs &quot;bad&quot; acting Garou if Philodox characters are to gain the Honor they need to advance. It needs Garou doing things like worshipping Hakaken on the side, engaging in man eating, making side deals with vampires, raiding another sept to steal their talens, abducting their kinfolk, and so on. Besides creating plot in general, it gives Philodox a chance to shine and earn the Honor renown they need.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-21T12:59:19-07:00","id":1551200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1430170-hakaken?p=1551199#post1551199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After a few online games, and running a tabletop chronicle of my own, I decided it was very hard for Philodox to earn Honor relative to Garou earning Glory and Wisdom. As a normal part of the game, there just seems to be many more opportunities to earn Glory and Wisdom than there are to earn Honor. As a result, I decided there needed to a be a certain level of scandalous or even criminal behavior among Garou so that Philodox (in particular, the other auspices usually can scrape up enough Honor that they need - at least until Elder rank) can pick up the Honor that they need. They need behavior they can expose and correct. They need disputes they can mediate. They need to speak truth to power even if it disrupts the sept or tribe to hear it.<br /> <br /> The game needs &quot;bad&quot; acting Garou if Philodox characters are to gain the Honor they need to advance. It needs Garou doing things like worshipping Hakaken on the side, engaging in man eating, making side deals with vampires, raiding another sept to steal their talens, abducting their kinfolk, and so on. Besides creating plot in general, it gives Philodox a chance to shine and earn the Honor renown they need.</div> </div> </div> </div>1000% agreed.<br /> <br /> Great ways to get some action for the half-moon:<br /> <br /> - you have to mediate a dispute<br /> <br /> - a Garou more senior than you has been found guilty of misbehaviour or a crime; it's been decided that you should be tested to see if you can decide a fitting punishment<br /> <br /> - the Sept's Rank 3 'rising star' casually commits a small misdemeanour in front of you, plays it off like it's no big deal, and becomes intimidating if pressed on the matter, leaving you with a problem of how you investigate further, who you tell, and if you're sensible you'll probably be wondering what ELSE this guy is up to<br /> <br /> - mock trial!<br /> <br /> - at Rank 3+, you become aware that a Rank 1 Garou has been punished overzealously by a Rank 2 Philodox, their proof-gathering and choice in punishment motivated by a grudge or bad blood or even bigotry, and now you have to untangle the knot of who did what and how they should be punished","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-21T13:05:29-07:00","id":1551201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1430170-hakaken?p=1551199#post1551199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What Gift is that and what sourcebook? I would guess it's a camp Gift of the Bringers of Light.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It is from the first ed Shadow Lord Tribe Book<br /> It is called Mask Taint, a level five Gift of the Lords of the Summit Camp - but actually I missremembered a bit, not Grandftaher but a Puppeteer Bane teaches it<br /> My mistake, sorry<br /> But my point still stands, Grandfather is not the purest of totems <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-21T19:02:55-07:00","id":1551208,"title":"","content":"If an ST is going to include Hakaken cults in some capacity in her chronicle, I think a brief biography would be in order. The basics of Hakaken's life would be known to some degree, not only among the Shadow Lords but also the Garou Nation. We're given some very basic information (he was a great ahroun, a leader, a member of the Masks camp, and was active for over forty years), but not much else. I think we can determine some other basic information.<br /> <br /> 1) He likely postdates the Black Spiral Dancers. Without the example of the White Howlers falling first, I don't see why Hakaken would want to prove he could overcome the Labyrinth.<br /> <br /> 2) He seems to postdate the Dark Ages game era. We don't get much information on the Black Spiral Dancers of this era, but no mention is made of Hakaken. While this might not have been intended in the sense a theoretical Dark Ages Book of the Wyrm or Dark Ages tribebook might have listed him, I'm going to use the absence of evidence to be evidence of absence.<br /> <br /> 3) I also don't think he's mentioned in any Wild West or Victorian Age sourcebook. However, I personally think this is rather late for an era when Hakaken was still around as a Gaian Garou or yet to be born. Forty years is a fairly long period, and he would have had an immense reputation. So despite the absence of evidence here as well, I'm going to say it makes more sense for him to have already lived and fallen by this time.<br /> <br /> 4) In the Chronicle of the Black Labyrinth, Hakaken is mentioned in a document written by the Laird of Demborough in the year of 1923. He is definitely an Incarna by then.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure if anything else can be stated to be definitive. Therefore, it seems Hakaken likely lived sometime between 1300-1800. That allows for a lot of possibilities. Knowing there are many options and none are better or worse than mine, I'll use in my chronicles that Hakaken was active during the time of the Great Turkish War (1683-1699). War raged all over Central Europe and the Balkans during this time (plus a lot of wars before and after), and wars can cover a lot of Garou activities that would normally be Veil breaking. It would provide a lot of opportunity for Hakaken to lead Shadow Lords to strike at their vampire enemies and other foes. A good time to earn a lot of Renown. It's also not a time and place combination covered by existing Shadow Lord history summaries in the tribebooks. So it's a good place to put something that won't seem to contradict any known canon.<br /> <br /> Finally, what type of name is Hakaken? It doesn't sound like a Garou name. And Hakaken seemed to immediately become an Incarna upon dancing the last spiral, so he technically never spent time as a Black Spiral Dancer. Is it the name of some great Wyrm servant he slew, and he became known by that? Is it some kind of occult puzzle or lore discovered in the Labyrnith? Was it an alias he used while in the Masks to generate fear amongst his enemies? I'll probably lean to the latter for now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-26T06:33:24-07:00","id":1551294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1430170-hakaken?p=1551208#post1551208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Finally, what type of name is Hakaken? It doesn't sound like a Garou name. And Hakaken seemed to immediately become an Incarna upon dancing the last spiral, so he technically never spent time as a Black Spiral Dancer. Is it the name of some great Wyrm servant he slew, and he became known by that? Is it some kind of occult puzzle or lore discovered in the Labyrnith? Was it an alias he used while in the Masks to generate fear amongst his enemies? I'll probably lean to the latter for now.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can use numerology to discovery what numbers are present in Hakaken name and then search what numbers and letters in petranic keys are equivalents.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10047-vis\u00e3o-de-\u00e1guia","name":"Vis\u00e3o-de-\u00c1guia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10047_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-26T15:39:19-07:00","id":1551304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vis\u00e3o-de-\u00c1guia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1430170-hakaken?p=1551294#post1551294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can use numerology to discovery what numbers are present in Hakaken name and then search what numbers and letters in petranic keys are equivalents.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's an interesting idea. Maybe Hakaken's identity was originally unknown when the Incarna first appeared, and skilled Theurges eventually deduced who he was and what had happened.<br /> <br /> Presumably &quot;Hakaken&quot; (by whatever Garou name he had) was known to have become lost in the Labyrinth and thought to have become fallen. However, nobody ever discovered a Black Spiral Dancer who could have been him. So the fate of &quot;Hakaken&quot; became an interesting mystery to the Garou (and especially Shadow Lords). When a new Wyrm Incarna of fear appeared, there may have been speculation if this was &quot;Hakaken&quot; because he was already known to be a master of using fear as a weapon. Eventually those skilled in Wyrm lore figured out the proper correspondences. Maybe the appearance of the name was Hakaken was first met through a propaganda/terror campaign undertaken by the new Incarna. It may have originally been considered some nonsense word, but as it was repeated the Garou decided it must have some significance.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-30T13:26:26-07:00","id":1551351,"title":"","content":"The Shadow Lords being the Shadow Lords, I\u2019d bet money on there being no small amount of uncertainty (and doubtless historical controversy) over which noteworthy Shadow Lord as the mortal form of Hakaken - I\u2019d bet the character\u2019s descent from the heights to dancing the Black Spiral would be the cause of more spin than anything this side of Penelope\u2019s unwelcome suitors - creating an ambiguity that would leave other tribes with enough to chasten the Shadow Lords in general, but not enough to throw more than generalised accusations against the tribe as a whole or any specific lineage thereof.<br /> <br /> To the best of my understanding, the Lords have a long history of being honest with themselves but almost nobody else: quite the antithesis of the Silver Fangs being generally named and shamed for their misdeeds.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, this sounds like an intriguing character on more thsn one level and I\u2019ll have to give him more thought: one thing that does occur to me is that Hakaken might fit rather well with the scenario (from APOCALYPSE, I think?) in which Grandfather Thunder takes out Whippoorwill and demands that the Black Spiral Dancers adopt him as their new Totem.<br /> <br /> That this is not a very good thing probably fits very neatly with Hakaken\u2019s ascension by damnation being a mixed-to-negative development, to say the least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-01T20:01:58-07:00","id":1551401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1430170-hakaken?p=1551351#post1551351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, this sounds like an intriguing character on more thsn one level and I\u2019ll have to give him more thought:</div> </div> </div> </div>That was definitely my opinion. His brief description as a pack totem in Book of the Wyrm 2e made me think he could be much more than just a pack totem for the Black Spiral Dancers. Not only could he be used as another enemy faction within the Shadow Lords as part of some other Wyrm cult, there was also room for &quot;legitimate&quot; Shadow Lords who are pro-Gaia, but nevertheless engage in what other tribes (but not them) consider to be enemy acts.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-09T08:58:47-07:00","id":1551541,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s always fun to find an obscurity than deserves more attention and do your best to mainline it (Also, if the Shadow Lords are good for nothing else, they\u2019re absolutely superb as the vehicles for stories that explore the line where Performative Villainy ends and actual Evil begins: the Shadow Lords talk a lot of smack about Silver Fangs and their endless ceremonies, rites and rituals but the Lords are far from innocent when it comes to loving the sound of their own voices and playing their own games whether or not anyone else can endure them).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-09T09:03:25-07:00","id":1551542,"title":"","content":"Incidentally, it has always struck me that The Margrave has always been cheated of some seriously awesome stories by the game line simply starting him in a position to dominate the most inveterately political and barely-scrupulous tribe in the Garou Nation as a reforming influence, rather than actually showing the sort of power politics, two-faced scheming and violent idealism required to make a Shadow Lord with some<br /> unusual ideas into one of the most powerful Garou this side of Armageddon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-07T06:58:13-07:00","id":1552140,"title":"","content":"Sorry to resurrect the topic, but I'm preparing my next chronicle and find something interesting in the book Chronicle of Black Labyrinth:<br /> <br /> <img title=\"image.png\" data-tempid=\"temp_1891_1751896558745_249\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1891\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1891\" data-thumb-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1891&amp;type=thumb\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"image.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-need-data-att-update js-lightbox-participant\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> So, follow the chart in the book, Hakaken it's in service (or influence) of Beast-of-War Wyrm and Hellbringer Maeljin.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10047-vis\u00e3o-de-\u00e1guia","name":"Vis\u00e3o-de-\u00c1guia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10047_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-08T02:42:23-07:00","id":1552190,"title":"","content":"I wonder if he\u2019s as unquestioningly loyal and obedient to them as the Shadow Lords are to the Silver Fangs?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-08T13:10:13-07:00","id":1552212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vis\u00e3o-de-\u00c1guia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1430170-hakaken?p=1552140#post1552140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, follow the chart in the book, Hakaken it's in service (or influence) of Beast-of-War Wyrm and Hellbringer Maeljin.</div> </div> </div> </div>Chronicle of the Black Labyrinth definitely puts Hakaken in service to the Beast of War, but that is because he serves the Urge Wyrm of Fear, Foebok. (He is the &quot;Heart of Fear&quot; after all.) Foebok has no Maeljin Incarna so Hakaken slots into that place. I think you are incorrect about Hellbringer because he serves Ba'ashkai, Urge Wyrm of Violence. Both Urge Wyrms are said to follow the Beast-of-War, but otherwise Hakaken does not have any relationship with Hellbringer.<br /> <br /> As an Incarna who directly serves an Urge Wyrm, I'm sure Hakaken is just as loyal as any of the Maeljin Incarna are to their Urge Wyrms. I can't remember off hand if the sourcebooks ever talk about that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-09T06:01:42-07:00","id":1552229,"title":"","content":"All of which strongly suggests that, whatever his original intent when dancing the Spiral, the Garou Hakaken was is well and truly lost to the Wyrm (and may, in fact, be a key element in the Wyrm\u2019s corruption of Grandfather Thunder in one version of the Apocalypse).<br /> <br /> On a vaguely-related note, I wonder if it makes sense to link Hakaken\u2019s rise to fame and glory with a period when the Silver Fangs made a serious mess of things - perhaps the era when King Aaron Everstone misused the Silver Crown and crushed the spirits of House Winter Snow, along with far too many of the defenders of the British Isles.<br /> <br /> Or perhaps just prior to that point - with the misfortunes of House Winter Snow the first triumph of the Wyrm corrupted Hakaken and his Black Spiral Dancers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-09T23:26:37-07:00","id":1552252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1430170-hakaken?p=1552229#post1552229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a vaguely-related note, I wonder if it makes sense to link Hakaken\u2019s rise to fame and glory with a period when the Silver Fangs made a serious mess of things - perhaps the era when King Aaron Everstone misused the Silver Crown and crushed the spirits of House Winter Snow, along with far too many of the defenders of the British Isles.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because there's very little canonical information about Hakaken, there's little to contradict it. Even if you are a strict canon purist, an ST can develop Hakaken in many different ways. There's nothing to suggest Hakaken is linked to any problems with the Silver Fangs, and there's no evidence to suggest he is not.<br /> <br /> In my above post on placing Hakaken is an actual historical time, I came to the conclusion he is most likely active sometime between 1300-1800, so a 17th century era (the era of King Aaron Everstone) would fit.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-10T03:15:11-07:00","id":1552257,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a>, I wasn\u2019t so much scratching my head over exact timing as I was questioning whether my idea served both characters and themes of their story arc as we understand it - obviously the newly fallen Hakaken needs a Win that makes him a suitable figure for the Black Spiral Dancers to venerate and really get him an \u2018In\u2019 with his own spiritual patron (Taking the Silver Crown off the board and reducing a whole House of Silver Fangs to Harano, whilst allowing the Dancers to tread a bloody measure all across the Isle of Britain wouod definitely do that), but his Big Coup should still leave <i>just</i> enough room for Shadow Lords of the most amoral or optimistic type to think \u201cWell he may have Danced the Spiral, but he\u2019s still Our Guy.\u201d<br /> <br /> On the other hand there\u2019s nothing quite like a Legend of the Garou fallen to Corruption to inspire extraordinary deeds - like claiming the Silver Crown - for Good and for Ill (One also wonders if placing Everstone\u2019s tragic arc after the execution of Charles the First but before the fall of James II &amp; VII would make the most sense? Having pogroms in the supernatural world in parallel with the \u2026 misfortunes of the 1660s in England might be symbolically apt, if nothing else*).<br /> <br /> <br /> *Heck, making the Restoration of the House of Stuart a key achievement of King Aaron Everstone, only for the Stuarts to become a completely divisive element in British politics seems horribly, horribly apt (Not least since the Netherlands and England being pitted against each other would probably divide House Winter Sky right down the middle - or at least split it\u2019s power base).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-11T10:16:35-07:00","id":1552286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1430170-hakaken?p=1552257#post1552257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">obviously the newly fallen Hakaken needs a Win that makes him a suitable figure for the Black Spiral Dancers to venerate and really get him an \u2018In\u2019 with his own spiritual patron (Taking the Silver Crown off the board and reducing a whole House of Silver Fangs to Harano, whilst allowing the Dancers to tread a bloody measure all across the Isle of Britain wouod definitely do that), but his Big Coup should still leave <i>just</i> enough room for Shadow Lords of the most amoral or optimistic type to think \u201cWell he may have Danced the Spiral, but he\u2019s still Our Guy.\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't necessarily think Hakaken &quot;needs a win&quot; so soon. After all, he just became a god. Sounds like a win to me. I would be a fine with a figure based entirely around fear to slowly build up his reputation. Creeping terror that slowly builds up over time can be, in many cases, better than a sudden shock.<br /> <br /> Other than a tiny blurb, I don't know much about the fall of House Winter Snow, but what I have read does not suggest anything that would involve &quot;the Heart of Fear&quot;. Hakaken is all about generating terror in your enemies, so much that the pack totem ban is that you cannot kill your enemies until you make them terrified. While one can certainly create new lore for one's chronicle that introduced some campaign of terror that happened during the fall of House Winter Snow, you could apply that to any other scenario as well.<br /> <br /> So while it's a possibility, I personally wouldn't do it. But with all things, everyone is going to have different tastes. Something I find compelling or fascinating might seem boring or ridiculous to someone else, and vice versa. If you really like that hook and can make that potential very compelling, definitely use it in your chronicles.<br /> <br /> However, I do agree that for the purposes of Hakaken cults within the Shadow Lords, that it'd be nice for the most amoral Shadow Lords to someone justify their veneration with the idea that Hakaken is still somehow on their side. However, I'd probably more likely go with the idea that the Masks camp (possibly other camps as well) was somehow involving his patronage in their own fear campaigns against the enemies of the tribe (and usually these enemies are outside the Nation). If Hakaken simply looks upon spiritual petitions of Shadow Lords with favor but not so much other tribes, that might be enough.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-14T09:00:15-07:00","id":1552371,"title":"","content":"My take was that Hakaken would have to do more than just dance the Black Spiral to become a Wyrmish demigod (Unless he had been secretly corrupt all throughout his career, which strikes me as less dramatically interesting than some sort of Nietzschean descent into the Abyss), hence my suggestion that he would need some sort of major triumph to become more than just another fallen hero (Especially where the Black Spiral Dancers were concerned).<br /> <br /> Your mentioning of the \u2018Heart of Fear\u2019 does strike me as suggesting a very plausible connection between this particular Wyrm spirit and the social upheavals of the English Civil War (and associated conflicts), the dramatic shifts from King to Parliament to Lord Protector to Restoration, the raw paranoia that fuelled the \u2018Popish Plot\u2019 and made Titus Oates hideously influential, along with any number of other convulsions and tensions across the British Isles in the mid to late 17th century.<br /> <br /> Quite frankly I\u2019m suggesting that it was the sense of a major Wyrmish threat growing at the same time that mortal society was tearing lumps out of itself (presumably inspiring or reflecting divisions within Garou society that mirrored and quite possibly fuelled divisions &amp; paranoia in mortal society) that drove King Aaron Everstone to seek one of the most powerful relics in Garou legend and much the same fears that moved him to make such poor use of it\u2019s power &amp; prestige by trying to FORCE the British Isles to be a model of Garou civilisation (Resulting in actions so shameful they drove his own House into mass Harano).<br /> <br /> Inspiring such Dread that the hero seeking to end your reign of terror becomes just another villain definitely strikes me as very much in keeping a character apparently characterised as a demigod of psychological warfare.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-14T12:40:56-07:00","id":1552385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1430170-hakaken?p=1552371#post1552371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> My take was that Hakaken would have to do more than just dance the Black Spiral to become a Wyrmish demigod</div> </div> </div> </div>Just to be clear, Hakaken did not just dance the Black Spiral, he was one of only two Garou to have ever completed the Ninth and final Circle of the Labyrinth. Passing (completing/succeeding) each circle (or spiral) of the Labyrinth is the equivalent of a rank challenge. Black Spiral Dancers who complete the first Circle are cliaths. Those very few who complete more than one usually top out at four or five because even great Garou only reach Athro or Elder. Completing the sixth circle, then, is equivalent to being a Legendary Garou. So we have to believe Hakaken (the other is the ruler of Malfeas, Number Two) completed multiple tests beyond the capabilities of even Legendary Garou. To complete the ninth circle, the Garou is supposed to defeat a manifestation of the Wyrm itself. That is why in WoD lore, completing the ninth circle raises you to the level of Incarna. It's an epic quest far beyond what any Garou should be able to do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4xgx4k83zzc\" data-code=\"4xgx4k83zzc\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/4xgx4k83zzc/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> Given that only two have ever succeeded (most never get to the ninth circle at all, and any others who did perished in the attempt), I'm fine with the story as is. However, this is rule zero territory so if you want something more, you can.<br /> <br /> Presumably the part about defeating a manifestation of the Wyrm at the ninth circle may be what prompted Hakaken to enter the Labyrinth in the first place. He might have thought it was a means by which he could destroy the Wyrm itself.<br /> <br /> In so far that the Garou has information concerning the Labyrinth's inner most levels, we might say such information could have come from Hakaken cultists who were given some information from Hakaken himself as it is part of his personal experience. I can imagine some Shadow Lords in the Lightbringer camp justifying their involvement in a Hakaken cult by &quot;winning&quot; such lore. I'm sure the Garou have other means by which to possibly learn of the innermost mysteries of the Spiral, but there can't be many of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-16T04:53:23-07:00","id":1552448,"title":"","content":"Aaaah, I wasn\u2019t actually aware of that background element: being WARHAMMER 40,000 trained, I\u2019ve always been very careful to avoid Books of Forbidden Lore.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> On a more serious note, destroying an element of the Wyrm only to replace it is such a perfectly Mythic way for a WEREWOLF hero to become a villainous demigod (and an excellent explanation for Hakaken being a figure of veneration for more \u2026 fringe elements of the Shadow Lords).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-16T05:28:21-07:00","id":1552450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1430170-hakaken?p=1552385#post1552385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In so far that the Garou has information concerning the Labyrinth's inner most levels, we might say such information could have come from Hakaken cultists who were given some information from Hakaken himself as it is part of his personal experience.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like to think it is actually an ellaborate lie - a bit like the Prophecy of the One in Matrix, crafted by a mastermind to fool the Garou<br /> (Or worse, it is actually the Truth)<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-16T11:01:32-07:00","id":1552453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1430170-hakaken?p=1552448#post1552448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aaaah, I wasn\u2019t actually aware of that background element: being WARHAMMER 40,000 trained, I\u2019ve always been very careful to avoid Books of Forbidden Lore.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems to be my specialty.<br /> <br /> In this case, the 2e Book of the Wyrm provides some fairly clear detail about this. However, it is also mentioned in the diagetic text of the Chronicle of the Black Labyrinth.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1430170-hakaken?p=1552450#post1552450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like to think it is actually an ellaborate lie - a bit like the Prophecy of the One in Matrix, crafted by a mastermind to fool the Garou (Or worse, it is actually the Truth)</div> </div> </div> </div>I suspect anything Hakaken provides about Wyrm lore (or any other source that provides it) has a mix of truth and lies to confuse the two and make the lies all the more believable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"